meta {
  name: Push without a token (refused)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{consumerUrl}}/push/{{mgmtTransferConsumerPid}}
  body: text
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: text/csv
}

body:text {
  day,celsius
  mon,12
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 401
}

docs {
  Since 1.1 (ADR 0027). The consumer's receiving route of push transfers,
  POST or PUT /push/{consumerPid}, on a connector with object storage and
  PORTITOR_PUSH_BUCKET. Only the provider's data plane has the token (the consumer
  connector keeps only its hash), so a request from here is refused: every refusal is
  the same 401 (no token, wrong or expired token, unknown transfer, a transfer that is
  not REQUESTED or STARTED). Without object storage the route does not exist (404).
  consumerUrl is the consumer connector's public URL; "Start push transfer" saves
  mgmtTransferConsumerPid. Debug: receiving.rs (crates/portitor-connector/src).
}
